\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces One hour of work with a coding agent, and the two records it leaves behind. The developer asked for three things and got a fourth (left). Git kept two commits whose fifteen hunks interleave all four requests (middle). The colours in that panel are ours, and git holds no record of which request produced which hunk, so a developer taking one request back out has to decide for each hunk whether it belongs to that request. \textsf  {sgt}{} recorded one edit per function and filed each under the request it came from (right), so the caching work is a set of six edits with a name, and the one function both the rate limiter and the cache touched is visible as such.}}{1}{figure.caption.1}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{fig:two-records}{{1}{1}{\FigOneCaption }{figure.caption.1}{}}
