\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces One hour of work with a coding agent, recorded four ways, with the same request removed from each. The unit a system records decides which sets a developer can name, and every row here is a design we think is correct for the constraints it was built under. Git and Darcs both bottom out at a line, so removing the caching means selecting lines. Jujutsu and Mercurial add a durable identity above the line, and it is the identity of a commit, so a squashed session carries one identity for all three requests. \textsf  {sgt}{} records one edit per function together with the request it was made for, which is the same information the developer supplied and never wrote down.}}{5}{figure.caption.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:granularity}{{2}{5}{\FigTwoCaption }{figure.caption.5}{}}
