\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces The ten operations, each drawn as the set before the command and the set after it. One line is one request and the marks on it are the edits filed under it, as in Figure\nonbreakingspace \ref {fig:two-records}, and a dotted outline is an edit the version no longer includes. No operation takes a hash. Every argument is a sentence the developer wrote, a branch name, or a function name. The right-hand column says what each operation costs, and we put it beside the command because a developer meets these costs on the first day.}}{10}{figure.caption.8}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:operations}{{5}{10}{\FigFourCaption }{figure.caption.8}{}}
